#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/bluetooth_espc201/10-iot_Bluetooth_environmental_monitor.rst:17
msgid "10. Bluetooth Environmental Monitor"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/bluetooth_espc201/10-iot_Bluetooth_environmental_monitor.rst:26
msgid "A DHT11 sensor measures the air, and the board pushes the two numbers to the phone every two seconds. This is the **first project that sends data the other way round**: until now the phone talked, the board listened. Here the board talks."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/bluetooth_espc201/10-iot_Bluetooth_environmental_monitor.rst:32
msgid "1. Build the Circuit"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/bluetooth_espc201/10-iot_Bluetooth_environmental_monitor.rst:36
msgid "The module draws a high current at start-up, so make sure the 9 V battery or an external power supply is plugged into the DC jack of the R4 Minima."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/bluetooth_espc201/10-iot_Bluetooth_environmental_monitor.rst:42
msgid ":ref:`cpn_uno`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/bluetooth_espc201/10-iot_Bluetooth_environmental_monitor.rst:43
msgid ":ref:`cpn_espc201`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/bluetooth_espc201/10-iot_Bluetooth_environmental_monitor.rst:44
msgid ":ref:`cpn_dht11`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/bluetooth_espc201/10-iot_Bluetooth_environmental_monitor.rst:48
msgid "2. Upload the Code"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/bluetooth_espc201/10-iot_Bluetooth_environmental_monitor.rst:50
msgid "Open the ``10-Bluetooth_environmental_monitor.ino`` file under the path of ``ultimate-sensor-kit\\code\\iot_project_espc201\\bluetooth\\10-Bluetooth_environmental_monitor``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/bluetooth_espc201/10-iot_Bluetooth_environmental_monitor.rst:54
msgid "Install the **DHT sensor library** (by Adafruit) and its dependency **Adafruit Unified Sensor** from the Library Manager."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/bluetooth_espc201/10-iot_Bluetooth_environmental_monitor.rst:57
msgid "Select **Arduino UNO R4 Minima** and the right port, then click **Upload**."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/bluetooth_espc201/10-iot_Bluetooth_environmental_monitor.rst:59
msgid "Open the Serial Monitor at **115200**. You should read:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/bluetooth_espc201/10-iot_Bluetooth_environmental_monitor.rst:70
msgid "If you read ``[!] no reply from the module``, the module is not answering on D0/D1 - check the four wires and the power supply."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/bluetooth_espc201/10-iot_Bluetooth_environmental_monitor.rst:74
msgid "This line is produced whether or not a phone is listening - useful, because it proves the sensor works before you go looking for a Bluetooth problem."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/bluetooth_espc201/10-iot_Bluetooth_environmental_monitor.rst:83
msgid "3. Watch the Data in LightBlue"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/bluetooth_espc201/10-iot_Bluetooth_environmental_monitor.rst:85
msgid "This time you do not write anything - you **subscribe**. Subscribing tells the phone to keep a characteristic open and show whatever arrives."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/bluetooth_espc201/10-iot_Bluetooth_environmental_monitor.rst:88
msgid "Open LightBlue, tap **Scan** and connect to **SunFounder-C2**."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/bluetooth_espc201/10-iot_Bluetooth_environmental_monitor.rst:90
msgid "Expand the service **0xA002** and open the characteristic **C305**."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/bluetooth_espc201/10-iot_Bluetooth_environmental_monitor.rst:92
msgid "Tap **Subscribe**. Numbers start to appear by themselves, twice per second:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/bluetooth_espc201/10-iot_Bluetooth_environmental_monitor.rst:99
msgid "The format is ``temperature,humidity``. ``27.00,45.00`` means 27 degrees and 45 % humidity. A comma separates them so the receiving side can split the line into two numbers."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/bluetooth_espc201/10-iot_Bluetooth_environmental_monitor.rst:103
msgid "Cover the sensor with your hand - the humidity number climbs within a few seconds."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/bluetooth_espc201/10-iot_Bluetooth_environmental_monitor.rst:107
msgid "If nothing arrives, check two things: that you opened **C305** (not C304), and that the Serial Monitor still shows ``Data to send:``. When the Serial Monitor is silent the problem is the sensor or its wiring, not Bluetooth."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/bluetooth_espc201/10-iot_Bluetooth_environmental_monitor.rst:113
msgid "4. Code explanation"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/bluetooth_espc201/10-iot_Bluetooth_environmental_monitor.rst:115
msgid "**Reading the sensor**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/bluetooth_espc201/10-iot_Bluetooth_environmental_monitor.rst:127
msgid "``isnan`` means \"is not a number\". A DHT11 that is not wired properly returns exactly that, so the sketch stops before it sends an empty line to the phone."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/bluetooth_espc201/10-iot_Bluetooth_environmental_monitor.rst:130
msgid "**One line, two values**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/bluetooth_espc201/10-iot_Bluetooth_environmental_monitor.rst:137
msgid "``bleSerial.println`` writes the text and a line ending, exactly like ``Serial.println``. ``BLEStream`` splits it into 20-byte chunks and sends each one as a **notification on C305** - that is why the phone has to subscribe."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/bluetooth_espc201/10-iot_Bluetooth_environmental_monitor.rst:141
msgid "**The two-second rhythm**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/bluetooth_espc201/10-iot_Bluetooth_environmental_monitor.rst:150
msgid "``delay`` is allowed here because this sketch does nothing else. In the Wi-Fi projects we avoided it, because Blynk had to be served all the time; Bluetooth needs no such background work."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/bluetooth_espc201/10-iot_Bluetooth_environmental_monitor.rst:154
msgid "**Why the board can talk without being asked**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/bluetooth_espc201/10-iot_Bluetooth_environmental_monitor.rst:156
msgid "A BLE notification only travels when the phone has subscribed to that characteristic. Nothing in the sketch checks \"is anybody listening\" - if nobody subscribed, the data simply goes nowhere. That is also why you see nothing in LightBlue until you tap **Subscribe**."
msgstr ""
